  "source": "one-continuous-master",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line-01",
      "text": "Pinocchio left the Tunny and followed a tiny light through the darkness.",
      "start": 0.127,
      "end": 4.553
    },
    {
      "id": "line-02",
      "text": "At a small table, an old man ate beside his final candle.",
      "start": 4.553,
      "end": 10.241
    },
    {
      "id": "line-03",
      "text": "The white-haired prisoner was Geppetto, the father Pinocchio had searched for.",
      "start": 10.241,
      "end": 16.175
    },
    {
      "id": "line-04",
      "text": "They embraced in disbelief, laughing and crying at the same time.",
      "start": 16.175,
      "end": 21.875
    },
    {
      "id": "line-05",
      "text": "Pinocchio poured out the entire story of his mistakes and misfortunes.",
      "start": 21.875,
      "end": 27.207
    },
    {
      "id": "line-06",
      "text": "Geppetto explained how the storm and Terrible Shark had swallowed him.",
      "start": 27.207,
      "end": 31.8
    },
    {
      "id": "line-07",
      "text": "He had survived inside the monster for two long years.",
      "start": 31.8,
      "end": 35.918
    },
    {
      "id": "line-08",
      "text": "Supplies from a swallowed merchant ship had provided food, candles, and matches.",
      "start": 35.918,
      "end": 42.908
    },
    {
      "id": "line-09",
      "text": "Now the food was gone, and the candle on the table was the last.",
      "start": 42.908,
      "end": 47.581
    },
    {
      "id": "line-10",
      "text": "Pinocchio insisted that they attempt an escape before darkness returned.",
      "start": 47.581,
      "end": 53.081
    },
    {
      "id": "line-11",
      "text": "Although Geppetto could not swim, Pinocchio promised to carry him.",
      "start": 53.081,
      "end": 58.203
    },
    {
      "id": "line-12",
      "text": "The ancient Shark's asthma forced it to sleep with its mouth open.",
      "start": 58.203,
      "end": 63.083
    },
    {
      "id": "line-13",
      "text": "Their first attempt failed when a sudden sneeze threw them backward.",
      "start": 63.083,
      "end": 68.223
    },
    {
      "id": "line-14",
      "text": "Pinocchio refused despair, took his father's hand, and climbed again.",
      "start": 68.223,
      "end": 73.703
    },
    {
      "id": "line-15",
      "text": "At the final row of teeth, Geppetto climbed onto his son's back.",
      "start": 73.703,
      "end": 78.888
    },
    {
      "id": "line-16",
      "text": "Pinocchio leaped into the moonlit water and began carrying them home.",
      "start": 78.888,
      "end": 83.68
    }
  ],
